-| `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK` | **OFF** when unset. Only an exact `1` enables the slot; `0`, unset, and every other value leave it disabled, so the Q1_0/Q2_0 arms of `ggml_repack_get_optimal_repack_type()` return `nullptr` and both types fall back to per-row `vec_dot`. **FLIPPED 2026-07-24** from ON-when-unset (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp`, `ggml_arifi_vnni_repack_enabled()`); the new predicate is the exact mirror of the old one. This **deliberately diverges from PrismML's upstream default, which is ON** — the measured reason is in the recommendation cell, and documenting exactly this kind of divergence is what this registry exists for. **Correction 2026-07-24:** the previous wording — that `=0` “restores the exact pre-slot behaviour” — was **false on x86**. Commit `c7645a0df` also replaced the x86 `ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0`, which sits **outside this toggle** (compile-time `__AVX512VNNI__`/`__AVXVNNI__` selection). `=0` therefore selected a *different* new kernel, not the pre-slot one. | Scope: the CPU repack *type-selection* for `GGML_TYPE_Q1_0` and `GGML_TYPE_Q2_0` only, inside `ggml_repack_get_optimal_repack_type()` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp`). ON lets those two types claim the `CPU_REPACK` buffer type and use the interleaved 4×8 GEMV/GEMM kernels (AVX512-VNNI on x86, NEON+DP on Arm); OFF falls back to per-row `vec_dot`. It does **not** touch Q4_0/Q4_K/Q8_0 repack, and is inert on any model containing no Q1_0/Q2_0 tensors. The x86 Q2_0 `vec_dot` fast path added alongside it is **not** covered by this toggle — see the default cell. | Only reachable at all for a **g64** Q1_0/Q2_0 model, and on a Vulkan-enabled build only with `--no-host`. **ADJUDICATED 2026-07-24 (bit-divergence round).** Bit-identity is **not achievable and was never the right bar** — proven against upstream's own repack types on this same binary (cost cell). The slot is now **correct and measured**. **DEFAULT OFF is IMPLEMENTED, not merely recommended** (flipped 2026-07-24, verified on a rebuilt binary — see the cost cell). The reason is unchanged: on a Vulkan-enabled build repacked weights lose GPU-offload eligibility and prompt processing regresses ~77–88%; on a CPU-only path the same slot is a **+327% to +442% prompt and +20% to +24% decode** win, so it stays compiled in and one `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=1` away. Set it to `1` for a CPU-only deployment; leave it unset everywhere else. The lane merges, not the executor. | **NaN FIXED (2026-07-24). Bit-divergence ADJUDICATED as INHERENT to the repack design, not a residual bug. Performance MEASURED (2026-07-24).**<br><br>**Root cause (one defect class, four sites).** PrismML's tree has `QK2_0 = 128`, so `QK2_0/QK8_0 = 4` and their kernels hardcode the activation-block stride as the literal `4`. This fork is canonical g64 (`QK2_0 = 64`, `ggml/src/ggml-common.h:187`), where the ratio is **2**. Every ported site that hardcoded `4` advanced the `block_q8_0` activation pointer twice as fast as its loop consumed, running past the packed activation buffer. **This is a downstream g64 integration defect, not a defect in PrismML's tree** — at g128 every one of these literals is correct.<br><br>**Fix A — the GEMM (4 lines, 2 files).** `ggml_gemm_q2_0_4x8_q8_0` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp:6664,6681`) and `ggml_gemm_q2_0_4x8_q8_0_generic` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp:2767,2786`): `(4 * y * nb)` → `(y * nb * (QK2_0 / QK8_0))` and `a_ptr + 4 * l + k` → `a_ptr + l * (QK2_0 / QK8_0) + k`, matching the form `ggml_gemv_q2_0_4x8_q8_0` already used correctly at `:6614`. Out-of-bounds `a_blk->d[m]` had been decoding as FP16 NaN and poisoning the FMA accumulator. The **Q1_0 arms were deliberately left alone**: `QK1_0 = 128`, so their hardcoded `4` is correct for this fork's current Q1 format — a portability hazard, not a present defect.<br><br>**Fix B — the control arm was itself broken (2 lines, separate commit).** The ported x86 `ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c`, added by `c7645a0d