cal prompt continues `“ the dog jumps over the lazy cat. What is the next…”` (6/6 identical), which the repacked arm tracks closely.<br><br>**Bit-identity: NOT achieved, and ADJUDICATED as INHERENT (2026-07-24).** The ON/OFF logprob divergence is real (both arms internally deterministic, 3/3 rolls each) but it is **a property of llama.cpp's repack design, not of this port**. Proven with an upstream-blessed control: four additional models were quantised from the *same* `qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-fp16.gguf` source with the *same* Q8_0 base and the *same* four tensors (`blk.0-3.ffn_down`, `4864x896`) carrying an **upstream** repack type instead of Q2_0, then run through the identical protocol on the identical binary. `--no-repack` was used as a uniform OFF for every arm and is byte-for-byte equivalent to `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=0` on the Q2_0 model (identical logprob fingerprint `3dea625c`, 3/3 rolls). Results, max absolute delta-logprob over 32 tokens: **ours Q2_0 4x8 = `0.061002`** (mean `0.0123761`, token-identical); **upstream Q2_K 8x8 = `0.140226`** (mean `0.0263535`, token-identical); **upstream Q4_K 8x8 = `1.39052`** (mean `0.328262`, and it **changes the generated text**). Upstream's own blessed repack types are therefore *less* faithful to their scalar paths than this port is to its own. Mechanism class is acknowledged upstream in-tree: `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp:210` comments that the repack activation quantiser is divided by `127.f` "to mirror results in quantize_row_q8_0" — a *mirror*, not an identity. **The prior demand for bit-identity was the wrong acceptance bar and is withdrawn.**<br><br>**Upstream 8x8 repack SEGFAULTS on this box — pre-existing, NOT this branch.** Three of the five upstream repack types could not be run at all: Q4_0 (`q4_0_8x8`), IQ4_NL (`iq4_nl_8x8`) and MXFP4 (`mxfp4_8x8`) all abort with `0xC0000005` ACCESS_VIOLATION once `--no-host` makes `CPU_REPACK` reachable, after the buffer is allocated (`CPU_REPACK model buffer size =