 decode figures in this row are g64 numbers and must not be read as g128 ones. The x86 Q2_0 `vec_dot` fast path added alongside it is **not** covered by this toggle — see the default cell. | Reachable for a **g64** Q1_0/Q2_0 model and, since 2026-07-29 (lane-110F), for a **g128** `Q2_0_G128` model, and on a Vulkan-enabled build only with `--no-host`. **ADJUDICATED 2026-07-24 (bit-divergence round).** Bit-identity is **not achievable and was never the right bar** — proven against upstream's own repack types on this same binary (cost cell). The slot is now **correct and measured**. **DEFAULT OFF is IMPLEMENTED, not merely recommended** (flipped 2026-07-24, verified on a rebuilt binary — see the cost cell). The reason is unchanged: on a Vulkan-enabled build repacked weights lose GPU-offload eligibility and prompt processing regresses ~77–88%; on a CPU-only path the same slot is a **+327% to +442% prompt and +20% to +24% decode** win, so it stays compiled in and one `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=1` away. Set it to `1` for a CPU-only deployment; leave it unset everywhere else. The lane merges, not the executor. | **NaN FIXED (2026-07-24). Bit-divergence ADJUDICATED as INHERENT to the repack design, not a residual bug. Performance MEASURED (2026-07-24).**<br><br>**Root cause (one defect class, four sites).** PrismML's tree has `QK2_0 = 128`, so `QK2_0/QK8_0 = 4` and their kernels hardcode the activation-block stride as the literal `4`. This fork is canonical g64 (`QK2_0 = 64`, `ggml/src/ggml-common.h:187`), where the ratio is **2**. Every ported site that hardcoded `4` advanced the `block_q8_0` activation pointer twice as fast as its loop consumed, running past the packed activation buffer. **This is a downstream g64 integration defect, not a defect in PrismML's tree** — at g128 every one of these literals is correct.<br><br>**Fix A — the GEMM (4 lines, 2 files).** `ggml_gemm_q2_0_4x8_q8_0` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp:6664,6681`) and `ggml_gemm_q2_0_4x8_q8_0_generic