m class is acknowledged upstream in-tree: `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp:210` comments that the repack activation quantiser is divided by `127.f` "to mirror results in quantize_row_q8_0" — a *mirror*, not an identity. **The prior demand for bit-identity was the wrong acceptance bar and is withdrawn.**<br><br>**Upstream 8x8 repack SEGFAULTS on this box — pre-existing, NOT this branch.** Three of the five upstream repack types could not be run at all: Q4_0 (`q4_0_8x8`), IQ4_NL (`iq4_nl_8x8`) and MXFP4 (`mxfp4_8x8`) all abort with `0xC0000005` ACCESS_VIOLATION once `--no-host` makes `CPU_REPACK` reachable, after the buffer is allocated (`CPU_REPACK model buffer size = 9.35 / 9.35 / 8.83 MiB`). gdb frame 0 is `ggml_gemv_q4_0_8x8_q8_0`, frame 1 `ggml::cpu::repack::tensor_traits<block_q4_0, 8ll, 8ll, (ggml_type)8>::compute_forward`, reached from `llama_decode` on a libgomp worker. **Attribution settled: stock upstream `llama-upstream-b10068` (`src/llama-upstream-b10068/build-vulkan/bin/llama-server.exe`) reproduces the identical crash on the identical model** — and this branch is strictly additive over its own base commit `f7c4d9d2c` (`git diff --numstat f7c4d9d2c..e32bf4149`: zero deletions in `repack.cpp`, `arch/x86/repack.cpp` and `arch/x86/quants.c`; the only deletion across the branch's nine commits is one `arch-fallback.h` alias). **Topology correction — RESOLVED 2026-07-24 (rebase round).** `f7c4d9d2c` is *not* master; it is the tag `pre-linearize-2026-07-24`, a merge commit on a parallel lineage. Master was then LINEARIZED to **`279f59f11`** (linear series, no fork merge commits); `67c83a6ec` is now an intermediate commit on that line, not the tip. The two lines diverged at `e70805586`. **The rebase is DONE:** `git rebase --onto master pre-linearize-2026-07-24 topic/vnni-repack` replayed all twelve commits with **zero conflicts**, and the resulting delta is byte-identical to the pre-rebase delta (same `git diff` blob hash `1330ce15`), so no content was lost or altered. The three dropped merge commits (`f7c4d9d2c`, `42c1b19be`, `e2ac92c40`) are gone from the branch ancestry and master is now a strict ancestor of it. **No conflict with `a54f6cae1` (Q2_0_G128 dispatch) arose, and none was possible:** that commit touches only `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp` (seven switch-case labels: add, add1, acc, out_prod, set, get_rows, clamp), a file this branch never modifies. No master-only commit touches any of the seven files this branch changes. The two mechanisms are disjoint in source and kept disjoint at runtime by the `GGML_TYPE_Q2_0_G128` early return at `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp:5164`. **Post-rebase sanity, re-measured on the rebased binary** (llama-server, `-ngl 0 --no-host -c 1024 -t 8 -v`, temp 0, top_k 1, seed 42, `cache_prompt` false): the NaN remains gone — `qwen2.5-0.5b-light-q8_0-4xffndownQ2_0-g64.gguf` ON returns coherent text with `CPU_REPACK model buffer size = 4.68 MiB`, OFF returns coherent text with **no** `CPU_REPACK` line at all, and `CPU_Mapped` is `625.75 MiB` in *both* arms (re-confirming the mmap-accounting correction below). The g128 path also still works: the native type-43 `Ternary-Bonsai-27B-Abliterated-LowDeg-Q2_0.g128.gguf` loads (`CPU_Mapped = 6822.71 MiB`, tensors reported as `q2_0_g128`), answers “The capital city of France is” with “ Paris. Paris is the capital city of France.”, aborts nowhere, and logs `token_embd.weight (q2_0_g128) (and 850 others) cannot be used with preferred buffer type CPU_REPACK, using CPU instead` with **no** `CPU_REPACK` buffer — the tripwire holds with the slot ON. **Gate default was ON when unset at the time of the measurements above** (`repack.cpp:5144-5150`), which did *not* match this row's own merge recommendation. **It has since been FLIPPED to OFF (2026-07-24)** and re-verified on a freshly built server binary (`recipe diff` PASS 309/309 first, then a `llama-server`-target build, exit 0), same protocol as above on `qwen2.5-0.5b-light-q8_0-4xffndownQ2_0-g64.gguf`, `-ngl 0 --no-host -c 1024 -t 8 -v`, fresh server per arm, reaped between arms, env flip only: **unset** produces **no** `load_tensors: CPU_REPACK model buffer size` line at all, **`=1`** produces `CPU_REPACK model buffer size = 4.68 MiB`. The loader's per-tensor fallback line appears in both arms and counts **290** ineligible tensors when unset against **286** with `=1` — the difference is exactly the four `blk.0-3.ffn_down` Q2_0 tensors the slot claims. Both arms return coherent text, no NaN, and `CPU_Mapped` is `625.75 MiB` in both (re-confirming the mmap-accounting correction above). Performance was **not** re-measured and did not need to be: the flip changes which branch an unset environment takes, not either kernel. Evidence: `research/local-inference/trial-evidence/110/vnni-default-flip/`. `--no-warmup` does not avoid the repack when the slot is on. The 4-wide/8-inter kernels — ours (`q2_0_4x8`, NB_COLS=4) and upstream's Q8_K pair (`q2_K_8x8`, `q4_K_8x8`) — run fine. Not this slot's defect; recorded for the lane.<br><br>**Performance: MEASURED 2026-07-24, from scratch.** All prior figures from this slot remain **void** (the `+58%` decode and `+354%` prompt gaps came from a NaN-poisoned ON arm; every pre-`2026-07-24` gap used the Fix-B baseline that read out of bounds). New protocol: llama-server per F-085, two models (`qwen2.5-0.5b-mixed-q8_0-ffnQ2_0-g64.gguf`, 72 Q2_0 tensors, `CPU_REPACK = 84.16 MiB`; and `qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-Q2_0-g64.gguf`, all-Q2_0, `CPU_REPACK = 95.98 MiB`; OFF arms show **no** `CPU_REPACK` line), `-ngl 0 --no-host -c 2048 -t 8`, 419-token prefill, `n_predict 128`, temp 0, top_k 1, seed 42, `cache_prompt` false, **three interleaved ON/OFF replicate pairs x 5 rolls**, fresh server per arm, reaped and verified gone between arms, free RAM `7.40–7.69 GB` at every launch. Timings read from `slot print_timing`; roll 1 of each arm dropped as a cold first request, leaving **n=9 per arm — every value listed, no means substituted**.<br>**CPU